      "name": null,
      "problem": "From top to bottom, what are the missing numbers in the ratio table below?\n\n| $4$ | $7$ |\n| --- | --- |\n| $12$ | $?$ |\n| $?$ | $35$ |\n\n$$\n\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "We start with the ratio $4:7$ and write it as a fraction:\n\n$$\n\\frac{4}{7}\n$$\n\nSo the numerator represents the left-hand entry ($4$), and the denominator represents the right-hand entry ($7$).\n\nWe can generate equivalent ratios by finding equivalent fractions:\n\n- To create a numerator of $12,$ we multiply the numerator and denominator of our fraction by $3:$\n\n$$\n\\frac{4\\times 3}{7\\times 3}=\\frac{12}{21}\n$$\n\n- To create a denominator of $35,$ we multiply the numerator and denominator of our fraction by $5:$\n\n$$\n\\frac{4\\times 5}{7\\times 5}=\\frac{20}{35}\n$$\n\nFinally, we fill in the ratio table:\n\n| $4$ | $7$ |\n| --- | --- |\n| $12$ | $21$ |\n| $20$ | $35$ |\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\nSo, from top to bottom, the missing numbers are $21$ and $20.$",
