      "dom_id": "question-101518",
      "name": null,
      "problem": "From top to bottom, what are the missing numbers in the ratio table below?\n\n| $?$ | $10$ |\n| --- | --- |\n| $3$ | $15$ |\n| $6$ | $?$ |\n\n$$\n\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "We start with the ratio $3:15$ and write it as a fraction:\n\n$$\n\\frac{3}{15}\n$$\n\nSo the numerator represents the left-hand entry ($3$), and the denominator represents the right-hand entry ($15$).\n\nWe can generate equivalent ratios by finding equivalent fractions:\n\n- To create a numerator of $6,$ we multiply the numerator and denominator of our fraction by $2:$\n\n$$\n\\frac{3\\times 2}{15\\times 2}=\\frac{6}{30}\n$$\n\n- To create a denominator of $10,$ we divide the numerator and denominator of the previous fraction by $3:$\n\n$$\n\\frac{6÷3}{30÷3}=\\frac{2}{10}\n$$\n\nFinally, we fill in the ratio table:\n\n| $2$ | $10$ |\n| --- | --- |\n| $3$ | $15$ |\n| $6$ | $30$ |\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\nSo, from top to bottom, the missing numbers are $2$ and $30.$",
